# Salon LD2410 and light sensor

## Device inventory

Reports LD2410 presence and BH1750 illuminance.

- **Firmware model** `ESP8266_LD2410_LIGHT`
- **Hardware** ESP8266. Custom NodeMCU build. Board vendor unknown.
- **Arduino build** [`nodemcuv2`](platformio.ini), configured version [`v1.2.0`](platformio.ini)

**Registry and broker snapshot** 19 November 2026, 09:01 CET.

| Location | DB room | DB display name | Registered sensors | Reported firmware | Arduino lib | OTA target | MQTT |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Madrid | Salon | `bcddc224-879f` | Light (analog/illuminance), Presencia (presence/presence) | `v1.2.0` in DB | `1.3.0` | `v1.2.0` | Connected |

This is the Salon presence and light-level unit. The separate Salon light relay runs [legacy Espruino firmware](../docs/legacy-devices/README.md#madrid-salon-light-relay).

[Device inventory index](../README.md#device-inventory)

## Sensors

The unit is sensor-only. It drives no relay.

| ID | Type | Topic | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `004_P` | presence | `004_P/state` (retained) | LD2410 on D1. Same shared `PRESENCE_SENSOR` as the other LD2410 devices. The cloud stores its history in `sensor_states`. |
| `003_L` | analog | `003_L/value` | BH1750 lux on D3/D4. Not published until the first valid sample. |
